// Compiler crash patterns found in V8 compiler optimization passes

// 1. CHECK/DCHECK failures in optimization passes
// - compiler/pipeline.cc: Many CHECK/DCHECK macros that can trigger crashes
// - compiler/simplified-lowering.cc: Extensive use of DCHECK, UNREACHABLE, CHECK
// - compiler/backend/register-allocator.cc: Many DCHECK and CHECK macros

// 2. Memory corruption patterns
// - compiler/heap-refs.cc:1119: "With heap corruption, a non-map object can be made to point to itself"
// - compiler/escape-analysis.h:134: "Reading out-of-bounds can only happen in unreachable code"
// - compiler/js-call-reducer.cc:8684: "out-of-bounds detection for DataViews"

// 3. Code generation crash patterns
// - compiler/backend/arm64/code-generator-arm64.cc:2331: "easier out-of-bounds detection"
// - compiler/backend/instruction-selector.cc:1483: "out-of-bounds memory access exception"
// - compiler/turboshaft/operations.h:2927: "Wasm trap handler for out-of-bounds accesses"

// 4. Recent crash fixes (2024-2025)
// - compiler/turboshaft/csa-late-escape-analysis-phase.cc (2025)
// - compiler/turboshaft/load-store-verification-reducer.h (2025)
// - compiler/turboshaft/wasm-debug-memory-lowering-phase.cc (2025)
// - compiler/common-utils.h/.cc (2025)
// - compiler/turboshaft/csa-effects-computation.h/.cc (2025)

// 5. Common crash triggers
// - AbortOptimization() calls in pipeline.cc for various bailout reasons
// - V8::FatalProcessOutOfMemory() for memory exhaustion
// - UNREACHABLE() macros for unexpected code paths
// - CHECK failures for invariant violations
